course: dictionary
lesson: 8178
title: Finding meaning from context: resource
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word like resource can have more than one meaning. Context means the words and sentences around it, and they leave clues. «Renewable resources, such as sunlight, wind and flowing water, are not used up.» The examples and the words «not used up» tell you a resource is something useful that people can use.
explain: «Natural resources are the things people take from nature to live: water, air, soil, wood, fish.» The list after the colon shows what natural resources are. So a natural resource is a useful thing from nature.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «useful things from nature» in place of «resources» in «Some resources renew themselves». If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. Remember that resource can also mean a person's skills and ideas that help them cope.
fact: A resource is something useful that you can use to help you do a job.
fact: Natural resources are useful things from nature, such as water, wood, oil, coal and soil.
fact: Renewable resources, like sunlight and wind, are not used up. Non-renewable resources, like coal and oil, can run out.
fact: In school, resources are learning materials such as books, websites and worksheets.
fact: Saving resources means not wasting water, paper or energy.
exercise: Which of these is a renewable resource? | Oil | Coal | Iron ore | *Sunlight
exercise: «Natural resources are the things people take from nature to live.» What are natural resources? | Skills that help people cope | *Useful things from nature, like water and wood | Money kept in a bank | Books and worksheets in a classroom
exercise: «Saving resources means not wasting water, paper or energy.» What does saving resources mean? | Buying new things every day | Throwing things away | Spending as much as you can | *Not wasting useful things
test: Which resource can run out? | Wind | *Coal | Flowing water | Sunlight
test: In school, what are resources? | Only the people who teach | Sports kit for the playground | *Learning materials such as books, websites and worksheets | Plants and trees
exam: Which sentence uses resource to mean a person's skills and ideas that help them cope? | The river is a resource that flows to the sea | *She used her calm thinking and quick ideas to cope with the problem | The shop sold a resource of pencils and paper | The forest had resources of wood and soil
